-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",68,{
[2145]="700001E2\n1\tTalk to Elrond\tMaster Elrond is at Imladris, far east of Elladan's camp of Thorenhad and above the Bruinen. Elladan has asked that you speak with his father about arranging an audience with the visiting Elves from Mirkwood, who might have some experience with creatures of the manner which you encountered.\n2\tTalk to Legolas in Rivendell\tLegolas is in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House. Master Elrond has told you of an Elf-prince named Legolas, currently staying in Imladris for a time. He hails from Mirkwood and may have some knowledge of the creature you faced in the Trollshaws.\n",
[2146]="70027380\n1\tTalk to Nai at the prison cave\tNai is guarding the captive emissary of Isengard in the prison-cave, south of Lheu Brenin and in the wall of the cliff to your left. Lheu Brenin has asked you to press the captive for information. First, you should speak to the guard Nai outside his cell.\n2\tTalk to Dondhreg\tNai has given you permission to enter the cell with Dondhreg to see if you can get any information from the captive emissary.\n3\tTalk to Lheu Brenin in Tûr Morva\tYou have spoken with Dondhreg, but if there was anything valuable in his words it will be up to Lheu Brenin to discern it.\n",
[2147]="70000FC2\n1\tTalk to Legolas in Rivendell and track down the wood-trolls\tLegolas is in Rivendell, in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House. The Elf-prince from Mirkwood, Legolas, is waiting to help you track down the Wood-trolls in the Trollshaws and defeat them. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tTalk to Legolas in Rivendell\tLegolas is in Rivendell, in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House. The Elf-prince from Mirkwood, Legolas, is waiting to speak with you about what the two of you saw in the lair of the wood-trolls.\n",
[2148]="7004429E\n1\tTalk to Peregrin Took and travel with him to your audience with Denethor\tPeregrin Took is in the Seventh Circle of the city. You have been summoned before Denethor, the Steward of Gondor. Peregrin Took has been charged with bringing you into Denethor's presence.\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir in besieged Minas Tirith, in the south-eastern area of the Second Circle\tMithrandir is in besieged Minas Tirith, in the south-eastern area of the Second Circle. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n",
[2149]="700001E3\n1\tTalk to Elrond\tMaster Elrond is within the Last Homely House. Legolas has asked you to go to Elrond at once and tell him what transpired in the lair of Taushakh, king of the Wood-trolls.\n",
[2150]="70027AB8\n1\tTalk to Catrin in Galtrev\tCatrin is in Galtrev, the Dunlending village in Pren Gwydh, west of Tâl Methedras. Lheu Brenin has asked you to travel through the lands of Dunland, seeing where the loyalties of the Dunlending clans lie and aiding those of like mind.\n2\tTalk to Wadu's Ghost in Pren Gwydh\t'Wadu's Ghost' has a camp to the west of Galtrev, in Pren Gwydh. Catrin told you of a girl that helped her with her resistance against the Ox-clan in Galtrev. This girl called herself 'Wadu's Ghost' and was asking about the Grey Company.\n",
[2151]="700442B4\n1\tTalk to Lamlor in the besieged Dome of the Sun and complete 'The Withered Tree'\030Talk to Ingold in the besieged city and complete 'Mad With Terror'\030Talk to Rathon in the besieged city and complete 'Fires in the City'\tLamlor can be found in the Dome of the Sun in besieged Minas Tirith. Ingold can be found atop the wall on the north end of the Third Circle in besieged Minas Tirith. Rathon can be found in the Sixth Circle near the street to the Citadel in besieged Minas Tirith. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n2\tTalk to Prince Imrahil in besieged Minas Tirith, atop the wall on the south-east end of the Second Circle\tPrince Imrahil is in besieged Minas Tirith, atop the wall on the south-east end of the Second Circle. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n",
[2152]="700001C2\n1\tTalk to Elrond\tElrond waits in the library on the upper floor of his house. Aragorn asked that you present yourself to Elrond, the master of the Last Homely House.\n",
[2153]="70014667\n1\tTalk to Bori\tBori is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek. Bróin has asked you to warn Bori against the overconfidence he fears the recovery of Zigilburk has awoken in the dwarves.\n2\tLocate and talk to Glúmur in Nud-melek\tGlúmur is in Nud-melek, overlooking Mazog's fortress. Bori has asked that you speak to his scout near Zabadgathol, and assist him in scouting out the area.\n3\tDefeat Pûlpum Flank-defender (total: 4)\030Defeat Pûlpum Foe-slayer (total: 4)\tZabadgathol, Mazog's fortress, is in Nud-melek. Bori has asked you to locate Zabadgathol and defeat some of Mazog's most loyal bodyguards, members of the Pûlpum.\n4\tSpeak to Glúmur\tGlúmur is located at the top of the stairs above the chamber in Nud-melek. You have defeated many of Mazog's loyal servants, the Pûlpum, and should return now to Glúmur.\n",
[2154]="700001E4\n1\tTalk to Glóin\tGlóin can be found at the camp at the top of the pass that leads from Rivendell into the Misty Mountains. Elrond suggested that you seek Glóin's aid in the hunt for the Nazgûl.\n",
[2155]="7002AB30\n1\tTalk to Saeradan by the fire at the camp in the Gravenwood\tSaeradan is at the camp in the Gravenwood, by the fire. Halbarad has decided that your path and the Grey Company's must now diverge, and you should say your good-byes to the Rangers.\n",
[2156]="7002AB31\n1\tTalk to Corunir on the path north-west of the camp in the Gravenwood\tCorunir was last seen down the path north-west of the camp in the Gravenwood, by a large boulder. You have spoken with Saeradan, and he told you to find Corunir and say good-bye.\n",
[2157]="7002AB32\n1\tTalk to Golodir in the shade of a boulder west of Corunir, in the Gravenwood\tGolodir is to the west of Corunir's location near the camp in the Gravenwood. Corunir wants you to speak with Golodir before you go.\n",
[2158]="7002AB33\n1\tTalk to Calenglad by the Tree of Tribute in the Gravenwood\tCalenglad is at the Tree of Tribute, in the Gravenwood. Golodir has sent you to say your good-byes to Calenglad.\n",
[2159]="7002AB34\n1\tTalk to Radanir on the road east of the Tree of Tribute, in the Gravenwood\tRadanir is on the road east of the Tree of Tribute, in the Gravenwood. Calenglad has told you to say your good-byes to Radanir, or the Rangers would never hear the end of it.\n",
[2160]="7002AB35\n1\tTalk to Prestadír by the winding road up to the camp in the Gravenwood\tPrestadír is to the north-east of Radanir, by the path that winds up to the camp in the Gravenwood. You should now say your good-byes to Prestadír.\n",
[2161]="7002AB36\n1\tTalk to Halbarad in the camp in the Gravenwood\tHalbarad is in the camp in the Gravenwood. You have made your farewells and should return now to Halbarad.\n",
[2162]="70045295\n1\tEnter the City Stables of Minas Tirith, in the First Circle\tThe City Stables are in the First Circle of Minas Tirith, opposite the main gate of the city. Mithrandir asked you to go to the City Stables of Minas Tirith and ask Lobordil for a rested steed to bring you past the enemy line, north into Talath Anor.\n2\tTalk to Lobordil in the City Stables\tLobordil is in the City Stables of Minas Tirith. Mithrandir asked you to speak to Lobordil in the City Stables, in order to procure a rested horse to bring you in search of Théoden and his Riders.\n3\tTalk to Duilin on the second level of the City Stables\tDuilin and Derufin are on the second level of the City Stables of Minas Tirith, up the stairs in the rear. Lobordil learned much from Duilin and Derufin that he should not have, and now should speak to them and learn who they spoke to about Gothmog.\n4\tSpeak hopeful words to worried soldiers in the City Stables (total: 4)\tWorried soldiers can be found throughout the City Stables of Minas Tirith. Duilin and Derufin have spread the rumour of Gothmog's invulnerability to death among the soldiers in the City Stables. You should do what you can to encourage the worried soldiers there, despite this troubling news.\n5\tTalk to Derufin on the second level of the City Stables\tDuilin and Derufin are on the second level of the City Stables of Minas Tirith, up the stairs in the rear. You spoke what hopeful words you could to the worried soldiers in the City Stables, but it seemed to be of no use.\n6\tTalk to Lobordil in the City Stables\tLobordil is in the City Stables of Minas Tirith. Despite the ill-advised rumour-spreading of the brothers of the Blackroot Vale, you still have a task set before you by Mithrandir: you must procure a rested steed from Lobordil in the City Stables, so you can seek the Rohirrim with all haste.\n",
[2163]="7002AB37\n1\tTravel to Grimbold's camp and speak with Grimbold\tGrimbold's camp is in the Heathfells, south-east of the Gravenwood. Halbarad wants you to offer your help to Grimbold, Théodred's second in command at the fords of the river Isen.\n2\tFind the map table in Grimbold's camp\030Talk to Trumbald on the road north of Grimbold's camp\030Talk to Cynstan on the west bank of the Ford of Isen\tThe map table is in the south-east corner of Grimbold's camp. Trumbald is on the road north of the camp. Cynstan is south of the camp, on the western bank of the ford. Grimbold has asked you to become acquainted with the layout of his camp and to speak with several of the scouts to learn of the situation here.\n3\tTalk to Théodred in Grimbold's camp\tThéodred is in Grimbold's camp, overseeing the preparations of his men. You have familiarized yourself with the situation in the Heathfells and should now find Théodred.\n",
[2164]="70045296\n1\tTravel north into Talath Anor in search of help\tLobordil provided you a rested horse to carry you with all haste along the road north of Minas Tirith in search of help.\n2\tTalk to Andothol where Hirgon lies, in Talath Anor\tYou have found the remains of Hirgon, and his mortally-wounded fellow soldier, north of Minas Tirith, in Talath Anor.\n3\tCross the bridge into Taur Drúadan, north-west of Hirgon's body\tYou should cross the bridge north-west of the bodies of Hirgon and Andothol, and decide what to do next.\n4\tEnter the wood to the south-west, in Taur Drúadan\tIf the road through the Beacon-marches is held by the Enemy, you will need to pass through the wood to the south-west to reach Théoden.\n5\tStudy the strange tracks beneath the eaves of the wood\tThere are strange tracks in the earth beneath the woods' canopy.\n6\tTravel south-west in search of more tracks\tThe strange tracks continue to the south-west within the wood.\n7\tTravel further south-west seeking more of the strange tracks\tThe strange tracks continue to the south-west within the wood, and the drumming has gotten louder.\n8\tTalk to the strange creature in the Drúadan Forest\tA strange squat creature watches you within the Drúadan Forest.\n",
[2165]="70000FCB\n1\tFind the goblin-camp\tThe goblins have many camps among the ridges of Pinnath Fenui, far to the east and north of Glóin's camp. Glóin told you that if you search for the goblins' camps in the Misty Mountains, you should find a goblin named Gurzmat. He appears to be their leader, and by defeating him, you should throw the goblins into disarray and perhaps find the trail of the Nazgûl.\n2\tDefeat Gurzmat\tGurzmat is somewhere deep within the goblin-camp that sprawls along the ridges of the Pinnath Fenui. Glóin told you that by defeating the goblin Gurzmat, you would throw the goblins into disarray and perhaps find the trail of the Nazgûl you seek.\n3\tTalk to Glóin\tGlóin is at his camp north of Rivendell. In defeating Gurzmat, you find him accompanied by hostile Dourhand Dwarves. Glóin should be made known of this development immediately.\n",
[2166]="700452A6\n1\tTalk to Khôr-buri-Ghân and tell him about yourself\tKhôr-buri-Ghân is in the Drúadan Forest. He has introduced himself as the son of the chief of the Wild Men, and wants to know who you are and what brings you to his lands.\n2\tTalk to Khôr-buri-Ghân and answer his question\tKhôr-buri-Ghân is in the Drúadan Forest. He has introduced himself as the son of the chief of the Wild Men, and wants to know if you are a friend of the gorgûn.\n3\tTalk to Khôr-buri-Ghân and tell him what you seek\tKhôr-buri-Ghân is in the Drúadan Forest. He has introduced himself as the son of the chief of the Wild Men, and wants to know what you are seeking and if it will prove harmful to the gorgûn.\n4\tFind the entrance to Drû Bhûta, the village of the Wild Men\tKhôr-buri-Ghân gave you directions to Drû Bhûta, the village of the Wild Men. He said: 'Drû Bhûta village to west. Must go north-west through rocks, across water. Then back south. Hidden path. Look for narrow path climbing south-west.' You hope you can follow that!\n5\tTalk to Khôr-buri-Ghân at the entrance to Drû Bhûta\tKhôr-buri-Ghân is waiting to welcome you to the village of Drû Bhûta.\n6\tTalk to Âm-buri-Sôl in Drû Bhûta\030Talk to Wêg-pulo-Ghûr in Drû Bhûta\030Talk to Mân-weni-Mhên in Drû Bhûta\tKhôr-buri-Ghân's fellow Wild Men can be found throughout their village of Drû Bhûta.\n7\tTalk to Khôr-buri-Ghân at the entrance to Drû Bhûta\tKhôr-buri-Ghân is at the entrance to Drû Bhûta.\n8\tTalk to Ghân-buri-Ghân\tGhân-buri-Ghân, the leader of the Wild Men, can be found in the village of Drû Bhûta.\n",
[2167]="7000113D\n1\tSearch the Gabilazan Cornerstone\tThe cornerstone containing the plans is located inside Gabilazan's Vault, located in one of the two passes east of Glóin's camp. Glóin's camp is north of Rivendell. Glóin told you that to learn how to access the secret entrance to Gabilazan's inner keep, you will need to take the plans for the fortress placed in its cornerstone.\n2\tBring the Gabilazan plans to Glóin\030Collect plans from Gabilazan cornerstone\tBring the Gabilazan plans to Glóin.\n",
[2168]="7002ACFF\n1\tTalk to Athelard on the eyot in the Isen\tAthelard is on the eyot in the middle of the river, south-east of Grimbold's camp. Théodred wants you to help Athelard with training some of the youths who have seen less combat.\n2\tTalk to a Rohirrim footman training on the eyot\030Talk to a Rohirrim archer training on the eyot\tRohirrim footmen and archers are training on the eyot in the Ford. Athelard has asked you to help train the footmen and archers under his command.\n3\tTalk to Athelard\tAthelard is on the eyot in the middle of the Isen, overseeing the training of his men. You have practiced sparring with the footmen and archers serving with Athelard and should tell him of your experience.\n4\tTalk to Rungar\tRungar is just to the north of Grimbold's camp, seeing to the training of riders under his command. Athelard has asked you to help Rungar with the training of his riders.\n5\tCollect thrown nets (total: 4)\tRiders are practicing their net-throwing down the hill to the east of Rungar. Rungar has asked you to collect some of the thrown nets and bring them back to him.\n6\tBring the nets to Rungar\tRungar is north of Grimbold's camp. You have collected some of the nets thrown by the riders and should bring them to Rungar.\n7\tTalk to Théodred in Grimbold's Camp\tThéodred is in Grimbold's camp, south of Rungar. Rungar has sent you to see Théodred.\n8\tTalk to Grimbold\tGrimbold is in his camp in the Heathfells. Théodred has told you to speak with Grimbold if you wish to help the Rohirrim with their plan to take Saruman by surprise.\n",
[2169]="700452A2\n1\tTalk to Khôr-buri-Ghân outside the Orc-camp near Amon Dîn\tKhôr-buri-Ghân has gone to the Orc-camp on the road north of the Drúadan Forest. Ghân-buri-Ghân has offered to help the Rohirrim if you will help his youngest son recover the body of his slain eldest.\n2\tEnter Maudhúl Grak and draw the enemy's eye\tKhôr-buri-Ghân asked you to draw the enemy's attention by entering the Orc-camp.\n3\tProceed further into Maudhúl Grak and draw the enemy's eye\tKhôr-buri-Ghân asked you to draw the enemy's attention by entering the Orc-camp, Maudhúl Grak.\n4\tTalk to Khôr-buri-Ghân in Maudhúl Grak\tKhôr-buri-Ghân is in the depths of Maudhúl Grak, waiting to speak with you.\n5\tReturn to Drû Bhûta\tYou should return to Drû Bhûta and speak with Ghân-buri-Ghân.\n6\tTalk to Ghân-buri-Ghân in Drû Bhûta\tGhân-buri-Ghân is in the village of Drû Bhûta. You entered Maudhúl Grak near Amon Dîn and recovered the body of Ghân-buri-Ghân's son, slain by Orcs. His other son, Khôr-buri-Ghân, has asked you to return to the Ghân and report your success.\n7\tTravel to the Blood-cloak in Drû Bhûta, on a rocky cliff on the eastern side of the huge waterfall\tThe Blood-cloak is to the east of the great waterfall in Drû Bhûta, atop a large rocky cliff. It is the location where the Wild Men perform their funerary rites.\n8\tTalk to Khôr-buri-Ghân at the Blood-cloak in Drû Bhûta\tThe Blood-cloak is to the east of the great waterfall in Drû Bhûta, atop a large rocky cliff. It is the location where the Wild Men perform their funerary rites.\n",
[2170]="7000113E\n1\tBring the key-stone to Glóin\030Collect the key-stone\tThe dwarf-vault that contains the key-stone is at Iskeld's Look-out, near the source of the Bruinen. Glóin is at his camp north of Rivendell. Glóin has asked you to retrieve a key-stone from an old dwarf-vault. The key-stone will allow you entry into the Dourhand-occupied dwarf-keep.\n",
[2171]="7002AD8E\n1\tExamine the map table and complete 'The Daring Strike, Dawn'\tThe map table is in Grimbold's camp. Study the map table in Grimbold's camp to begin Prince Théodred's attack.\n2\tExamine the map table and complete 'The Daring Strike, Mid-day'\tThe map table is in Grimbold's camp. Study the map table in Grimbold's camp to continue Prince Théodred's attack.\n3\tExamine the map table and complete 'Battle of the Ford, Afternoon'\tThe map table is in Grimbold's camp. Study the map table in Grimbold's camp to continue Prince Théodred's retreat.\n4\tExamine the map table and complete 'Battle of the Ford, Sunset'\tThe map table is in Grimbold's camp. Study the map table in Grimbold's camp to continue Prince Théodred's retreat.\n5\tExamine the map table and complete 'The Prince of Rohan, Night'\tThe map table is in Grimbold's camp. Study the map table in Grimbold's camp to witness the aftermath of the battle.\n6\tTalk to Grimbold in his camp in the Heathfells\tGrimbold is in his camp by the Ford of Isen. Grimbold is waiting to speak with you following the events of the day.\n",
[2172]="7000113F\n1\tSpeak to Gimli in Rivendell\tGimli is in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House. When you have gathered a fellowship, seek out Gimli, and he will accompany you to the dwarf-keep where the Nazgûl and Skorgrím may be hiding. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tTalk to Glóin\tGlóin is at his camp north of Rivendell. The Nazgûl left the dwarf-keep, commanding Skorgrím to slay you. Fortunately, you were able to defeat Skorgrím, but a fell spirit emerged from his corpse and cursed the Longbeards before vanishing. You should tell Glóin all that has transpired.\n",
[2173]="700452A3\n1\tFind the entrance to the Rohirrim encampment west of Eilenach, along the road\tThe Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan is located west of the hill of Eilenach, along the road.\n2\tTalk to Wídfara on the edge of the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan\tWídfara is at the entrance to the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan.\n3\tTalk to Herubrand in the western reach of the encampment in Taur Drúadan\030Talk to Fastred in the north-eastern reach of the encampment in Taur Drúadan\030Talk to Grimbold in the centre of the encampment in Taur Drúadan\030Talk to Elfmar in the eastern reach of the encampment in Taur Drúadan\tWídfara thought you should visit many of the Riders encamped in Taur Drúadan, believing it would lift their spirits.\n4\tTalk to Thrymm Red-beard in the south-eastern reaches of the encampment in Taur Drúadan\tThrymm Red-beard and his Éored are on a rise in the south-eastern reaches of the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan.\n5\tTalk to Harding in the north-eastern reaches of the encampment in Taur Drúadan\tHarding is in the north-eastern reaches of the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan.\n6\tTalk to Ingbert in the eastern area of the encampment in Taur Drúadan\tHarding told you to speak to Ingbert at his tents to the west, in the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan.\n",
[2174]="70000FD2\n1\tScout the borders of Helegrod\tHelegrod is north of Glóin's camp. The outer treasury is near Nan Gongarag. Glóin thinks you may be able to learn what the Nazgûl's plan for Helegrod is by scouting the borders of that abandoned hall for the entrance to the treasury. He warned you not to enter Helegrod itself, for it is guarded too strongly by dark things.\n2\tBring the Sigil of Drugoth to Glóin\030Search one of the wights\tHelegrod is north of Glóin's camp. At the entrance to Helegrod's treasury you encountered wights. You should defeat one and search its remains for some clue as to what brought it here.\n",
[2175]="700452A4\n1\tTalk to Horn in the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan\tHorn is in the clearing where his father Ingbert's men are resting before the ride continues. Ingbert claims that his son has finally come to his senses, and challenged you to find out for yourself.\n2\tTalk to Horn in the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan\tHorn is in the clearing where his father Ingbert's men are resting before the ride continues.\n3\tTalk to Gléowine in the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan\tGléowine is near Elfhelm's tent in the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan. Horn has asked you to speak with Gléowine if you want to hear his side of the argument.\n4\tTalk to Elfhelm in the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan\tElfhelm is not far from his tent in the Rohirrim encampment in Taur Drúadan. Elfhelm has listened to your conversation with Gléowine, and has something of his own to add.\n5\tFind the person of whom Elfhelm cryptically spoke\tElfhelm said someone with something to add to the subject of duty is just to the west, and you should find this person if you can keep the meeting a secret.\n",
[2176]="700001E5\n1\tBring the Sigil of Drugoth to Master Elrond\tElrond is in the library of Imladris. Glóin has asked you to speak with Elrond about what you have discovered outside of Helegrod's treasury.\n",
})
